<title>ZIMBABWE: Zimbabwe's Cairns lifts half-yr shr.</title>
<headline>Zimbabwe's Cairns lifts half-yr shr.</headline>
<dateline>HARARE 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half-yr ended February 28.</p>
<p>	     (million Zimbabwe dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)			 41.9    vs   31.8</p>
<p>    Div (cts)			 12.0    vs   10.0</p>
<p>    Operating profit		26.9    vs   19.3</p>
<p>    Interest payable		 2.8    vs    3.0</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		  24.1    vs   16.3</p>
<p>    Taxation			   9.6    vs    5.9</p>
<p>    After-tax profit		14.4    vs   10.4</p>
<p>    Turnover			  234.1   vs   172.0</p>
<p>Div payable May 27</p>
<p>on register April 25.</p>
<p>Full name: Cairns Holdings Limited</p>
<p>NOTE:- The company said while supply conditions had been adversely affected by recent heavy rains, it remained optimistic that it would exceed its year end earnings forecast of Z$25.5 million.</p>
<p>--Harare Newsroom: +263-4 72 52 27/8/9--</p>
</text>
